/* Generated by build/build-data.mjs from sources/word-families.json — do not edit by hand. */
window.POP_FAMILIES = [{"id":"power","name":"Power, Strength & Authority","lang":"Greek","english":["power","strength","might","authority","working","dominion"],"intro":"English Bibles say ‘power’ for at least six different Greek words. Paul stacks four of them in one breath in Ephesians 1:19 and lists four ranks of spiritual power in Ephesians 1:21. In Colossians 1:13 the WEB's ‘power of darkness’ is not δύναμις at all but ἐξουσία — authority. Knowing which word stands behind ‘power’ tells you what kind of power is meant.","members":[{"strongs":"G1411","sense":"Inherent ability — the capacity to act and to accomplish. Also used for miracles (‘mighty works’), because a miracle is power on display.","anchor":"Acts 1:8","en":"power","text":"But you will receive power when the Holy Spirit has come upon you. You will be witnesses to me in Jerusalem, in all Judea and Samaria, and to the uttermost parts of the earth.”"},{"strongs":"G1753","sense":"Power in operation — energy actually being exerted. Used in the New Testament almost only of God's (or Satan's) power at work.","anchor":"Ephesians 3:7","en":"working","text":"of which I was made a servant, according to the gift of that grace of God which was given me according to the working of his power."},{"strongs":"G1754","sense":"To be at work, to operate effectively — the verb of ἐνέργεια: God's power actively working in His people and His word.","anchor":"Philippians 2:13","en":"works","text":"For it is God who works in you both to will and to work, for his good pleasure."},{"strongs":"G2904","sense":"Dominion-strength — power that prevails and rules. Often in doxologies: to Him be the power forever.","anchor":"Hebrews 2:14","en":"power","text":"Since then the children have shared in flesh and blood, he also himself in the same way partook of the same, that through death he might bring to nothing him who had the power of death, that is, the devil,"},{"strongs":"G2479","sense":"Strength, force, might — the raw capacity a person possesses, as in loving God with all your strength.","anchor":"Mark 12:30","en":"strength","text":"you shall love the Lord your God with all your heart, and with all your soul, and with all your mind, and with all your strength.’ This is the first commandment."},{"strongs":"G1849","sense":"Authority — the right to act, delegated or given. Not how strong you are, but what you are authorised to do.","anchor":"Matthew 28:18","en":"authority","text":"Jesus came to them and spoke to them, saying, “All authority has been given to me in heaven and on earth."},{"strongs":"G746","sense":"Rule, principality — a position of first rank (also means ‘beginning’). Used for ruling powers, human and spiritual.","anchor":"Ephesians 1:21","en":"rule","text":"far above all rule, and authority, and power, and dominion, and every name that is named, not only in this age, but also in that which is to come."}]},{"id":"time","name":"Time, Season & Age","lang":"Greek","english":["time","season","hour","age","day"],"intro":"Greek separates kinds of time that English blurs together. Acts 1:7 sets ‘times’ (χρόνος) beside ‘seasons’ (καιρός): length of time and the right moment. In John 17:1 the WEB's ‘the time has come’ is ὥρα, the appointed hour.","members":[{"strongs":"G5550","sense":"Chronological time — duration, a span of time, time as it passes (the root of ‘chronology’).","anchor":"Galatians 4:4","en":"time","text":"But when the fullness of the time came, God sent out his Son, born to a woman, born under the law,"},{"strongs":"G2540","sense":"The right moment — a season, an opportunity, a decisive time that must be seized.","anchor":"Mark 1:15","en":"time","text":"and saying, “The time is fulfilled, and God’s Kingdom is at hand! Repent, and believe in the Good News.”"},{"strongs":"G5610","sense":"Hour — literally an hour, and in John the appointed hour of Jesus' death and glory.","anchor":"John 17:1","en":"time","text":"Jesus said these things, and lifting up his eyes to heaven, he said, “Father, the time has come. Glorify your Son, that your Son may also glorify you;"},{"strongs":"G165","sense":"Age, era — a long period with its own character (‘this present evil age’), and in the plural, eternity.","anchor":"Galatians 1:4","en":"age","text":"who gave himself for our sins, that he might deliver us out of this present evil age, according to the will of our God and Father—"},{"strongs":"G2250","sense":"Day — a literal day, and ‘the day’ of the Lord's return and judgment.","anchor":"1 Thessalonians 5:2","en":"day","text":"For you yourselves know well that the day of the Lord comes like a thief in the night."}]},{"id":"love","name":"Love & Affection","lang":"Greek","english":["love","affection","affectionate"],"intro":"In John 21:15 Jesus asks with ἀγαπάω and Peter answers with φιλέω; the WEB marks the difference as ‘love’ and ‘affection’. The common Greek word ἔρως (romantic desire) never appears in the New Testament.","members":[{"strongs":"G25","sense":"To love by choice and commitment — self-giving love that seeks the other's good, the love God shows.","anchor":"John 3:16","en":"loved","text":"For God so loved the world, that he gave his one and only Son, that whoever believes in him should not perish, but have eternal life."},{"strongs":"G26","sense":"Love (noun) — the self-giving love described in 1 Corinthians 13 and poured out by God.","anchor":"1 Corinthians 13:4","en":"love","text":"Love is patient and is kind; love doesn’t envy. Love doesn’t brag, is not proud,"},{"strongs":"G5368","sense":"To be fond of, have warm affection for — the love of friends (φίλος, friend).","anchor":"John 21:15","en":"affection","text":"So when they had eaten their breakfast, Jesus said to Simon Peter, “Simon, son of Jonah, do you love me more than these?” He said to him, “Yes, Lord; you know that I have affection for you.” He said to him, “Feed my lambs.”"},{"strongs":"G5360","sense":"Brotherly love — the warm love of brothers and sisters, applied to the family of believers.","anchor":"Romans 12:10","en":"love","text":"In love of the brothers be tenderly affectionate to one another; in honor preferring one another;"},{"strongs":"G5387","sense":"Tenderly affectionate — the natural, family kind of love (στοργή) between relatives.","anchor":"Romans 12:10","en":"affectionate","text":"In love of the brothers be tenderly affectionate to one another; in honor preferring one another;"}]},{"id":"know","name":"Know & Knowledge","lang":"Greek","english":["know","knowledge"],"intro":"‘Know’ in English can mean knowing a fact or knowing a person. Greek usually keeps these apart. 1 Corinthians 8:1 has both οἶδα (‘we know’) and γνῶσις (‘knowledge’) in one sentence.","members":[{"strongs":"G1097","sense":"To come to know by experience and relationship — knowing a person, not just facts about them.","anchor":"John 17:3","en":"know","text":"This is eternal life, that they should know you, the only true God, and him whom you sent, Jesus Christ."},{"strongs":"G1492","sense":"To know as settled fact, to perceive (Strong's files the past-tense ‘saw’ under this number too).","anchor":"Romans 8:28","en":"know","text":"We know that all things work together for good for those who love God, to those who are called according to his purpose."},{"strongs":"G1108","sense":"Knowledge — what is known; at Corinth, knowledge that puffed people up.","anchor":"1 Corinthians 8:1","en":"knowledge","text":"Now concerning things sacrificed to idols: We know that we all have knowledge. Knowledge puffs up, but love builds up."},{"strongs":"G1922","sense":"Full, precise knowledge — ἐπί (upon) + γνῶσις: knowledge that grips and transforms.","anchor":"Colossians 1:9","en":"knowledge","text":"For this cause, we also, since the day we heard this, don’t cease praying and making requests for you, that you may be filled with the knowledge of his will in all spiritual wisdom and understanding,"}]},{"id":"word","name":"Word & Utterance","lang":"Greek","english":["word"],"intro":"Both λόγος and ῥῆμα are translated ‘word’. The sword of the Spirit in Ephesians 6:17 is the ῥῆμα of God — the word spoken.","members":[{"strongs":"G3056","sense":"Word, message, reasoned account — and Jesus Himself, the Word.","anchor":"John 1:1","en":"Word","text":"In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with God, and the Word was God."},{"strongs":"G4487","sense":"A spoken word, an utterance — a particular saying that proceeds out of a mouth.","anchor":"Ephesians 6:17","en":"word","text":"And take the helmet of salvation, and the sword of the Spirit, which is the word of God;"}]},{"id":"life","name":"Life & Soul","lang":"Greek","english":["life","live","soul"],"intro":"‘Life’ in English Bibles can stand for three Greek words: life itself, the means of living, and the individual soul. John 10:10–11 uses two of them a sentence apart.","members":[{"strongs":"G2222","sense":"Life itself — the life that comes from God; ‘eternal life’.","anchor":"John 10:10","en":"life","text":"The thief only comes to steal, kill, and destroy. I came that they may have life, and may have it abundantly."},{"strongs":"G979","sense":"Livelihood, the means and course of earthly life — possessions, lifestyle.","anchor":"1 John 2:16","en":"life","text":"For all that is in the world, the lust of the flesh, the lust of the eyes, and the pride of life, isn’t the Father’s, but is the world’s."},{"strongs":"G5590","sense":"Soul — the individual self, the person's own life (laid down by the Good Shepherd).","anchor":"John 10:11","en":"life","text":"I am the good shepherd. The good shepherd lays down his life for the sheep."}]},{"id":"new","name":"New","lang":"Greek","english":["new"],"intro":"Greek has one word for ‘new in kind’ and another for ‘new in time’.","members":[{"strongs":"G2537","sense":"New in quality — fresh, unprecedented, of a different kind (a new creation).","anchor":"2 Corinthians 5:17","en":"new","text":"Therefore if anyone is in Christ, he is a new creation. The old things have passed away. Behold, all things have become new."},{"strongs":"G3501","sense":"New in time — recent, young (the new man, freshly come into being).","anchor":"Colossians 3:10","en":"new","text":"and have put on the new man, who is being renewed in knowledge after the image of his Creator,"}]},{"id":"another","name":"Another & Different","lang":"Greek","english":["another","different"],"intro":"Galatians 1:6–7 uses both words: a ‘different’ (ἕτερος) gospel, which is not ‘another’ (ἄλλος) gospel at all.","members":[{"strongs":"G243","sense":"Another of the same kind — Jesus promises another Counselor like Himself.","anchor":"John 14:16","en":"another","text":"I will pray to the Father, and he will give you another Counselor, that he may be with you forever,—"},{"strongs":"G2087","sense":"Another of a different kind — something other, different in nature.","anchor":"Galatians 1:6","en":"different","text":"I marvel that you are so quickly deserting him who called you in the grace of Christ to a different “good news”;"}]},{"id":"world","name":"World, Age & Earth","lang":"Greek","english":["world","earth"],"intro":"‘World’ in English Bibles can mean the created order, humanity, the system opposed to God, an age, or the inhabited lands. Romans 12:2's ‘this world’ is αἰών — this age.","members":[{"strongs":"G2889","sense":"The ordered world — creation, humanity, and often the world-system that rejects God.","anchor":"1 John 2:15","en":"world","text":"Don’t love the world or the things that are in the world. If anyone loves the world, the Father’s love isn’t in him."},{"strongs":"G165","sense":"The age — the present era with its values and spirit.","anchor":"Romans 12:2","en":"world","text":"Don’t be conformed to this world, but be transformed by the renewing of your mind, so that you may prove what is the good, well-pleasing, and perfect will of God."},{"strongs":"G3625","sense":"The inhabited earth — the civilised, populated world (often the Roman Empire).","anchor":"Luke 2:1","en":"world","text":"Now in those days, a decree went out from Caesar Augustus that all the world should be enrolled."},{"strongs":"G1093","sense":"Earth, land, ground — the physical earth or a territory.","anchor":"Matthew 5:5","en":"earth","text":"Blessed are the gentle, for they shall inherit the earth."}]},{"id":"servant","name":"Servant","lang":"Greek","english":["servant","servants"],"intro":"‘Servant’ can translate five Greek words, each describing a different relationship of service.","members":[{"strongs":"G1401","sense":"Bondservant, slave — one who belongs wholly to a master.","anchor":"Romans 1:1","en":"servant","text":"Paul, a servant of Jesus Christ, called to be an apostle, set apart for the Good News of God,"},{"strongs":"G1249","sense":"Servant in action — one who serves others, a minister (the root of ‘deacon’).","anchor":"Mark 10:43","en":"servant","text":"But it shall not be so among you, but whoever wants to become great among you shall be your servant."},{"strongs":"G5257","sense":"Assistant, attendant — originally an ‘under-rower’ taking orders from above.","anchor":"1 Corinthians 4:1","en":"servants","text":"So let a man think of us as Christ’s servants, and stewards of God’s mysteries."},{"strongs":"G3610","sense":"Household servant — a domestic who lives in the master's house.","anchor":"Luke 16:13","en":"servant","text":"No servant can serve two masters, for either he will hate the one, and love the other; or else he will hold to one, and despise the other. You aren’t able to serve God and Mammon.”"},{"strongs":"G3011","sense":"Public or sacred servant — one who carries out a priestly or public service.","anchor":"Romans 15:16","en":"servant","text":"that I should be a servant of Christ Jesus to the Gentiles, serving as a priest of the Good News of God, that the offering up of the Gentiles might be made acceptable, sanctified by the Holy Spirit."}]},{"id":"work","name":"Work, Labour & Toil","lang":"Greek","english":["work","works","labor","toil","travail","working"],"intro":"English ‘work’ and ‘labour’ cover several Greek words. 1 Thessalonians 1:3 sets ἔργον (work) beside κόπος (labour to the point of exhaustion), and 2:9 adds μόχθος (hardship) and ἐργάζομαι (working). Revelation 2:2 praises ‘works’ and ‘toil’ in a church that had left its first love.","members":[{"strongs":"G2041","sense":"Work, deed — an action or task, what a person does (the root of ‘ergonomics’).","anchor":"1 Thessalonians 1:3","en":"work","text":"remembering without ceasing your work of faith and labor of love and perseverance of hope in our Lord Jesus Christ, before our God and Father."},{"strongs":"G2873","sense":"Labour, toil — hard work that wears you out; effort to the point of weariness.","anchor":"1 Thessalonians 1:3","en":"labor","text":"remembering without ceasing your work of faith and labor of love and perseverance of hope in our Lord Jesus Christ, before our God and Father."},{"strongs":"G2872","sense":"To labour, to toil to weariness — the verb of κόπος, used of those who work hard in ministry.","anchor":"1 Thessalonians 5:12","en":"labor","text":"But we beg you, brothers, to know those who labor among you, and are over you in the Lord, and admonish you,"},{"strongs":"G3449","sense":"Hardship, travail — exhausting toil with difficulty and struggle.","anchor":"1 Thessalonians 2:9","en":"travail","text":"For you remember, brothers, our labor and travail; for working night and day, that we might not burden any of you, we preached to you the Good News of God."},{"strongs":"G2038","sense":"To work — to do a job, to earn a living by labour.","anchor":"1 Thessalonians 4:11","en":"work","text":"and that you make it your ambition to lead a quiet life, and to do your own business, and to work with your own hands, even as we instructed you;"}]},{"id":"sin","name":"Sin, Transgression & Debt","lang":"Greek","english":["sin","sins","transgression","transgressions","trespass","lawlessness","debts"],"intro":"The New Testament describes sin from several angles: missing the mark, a false step, crossing a line, living without law, and owing a debt. Ephesians 2:1 uses two of these words together.","members":[{"strongs":"G266","sense":"Missing the mark — falling short of God's standard; the general word for sin.","anchor":"Romans 6:23","en":"sin","text":"For the wages of sin is death, but the free gift of God is eternal life in Christ Jesus our Lord."},{"strongs":"G3900","sense":"A false step, a fall beside the path (often translated ‘trespass’ or ‘transgression’).","anchor":"Ephesians 2:1","en":"transgressions","text":"You were made alive when you were dead in transgressions and sins,"},{"strongs":"G3847","sense":"Transgression — stepping over a known line, breaking a stated command.","anchor":"Galatians 3:19","en":"transgressions","text":"Then why is there the law? It was added because of transgressions, until the offspring should come to whom the promise has been made. It was ordained through angels by the hand of a mediator."},{"strongs":"G458","sense":"Lawlessness — living as if no law applied; rebellion against God's rule.","anchor":"1 John 3:4","en":"lawlessness","text":"Everyone who sins also commits lawlessness. Sin is lawlessness."},{"strongs":"G3783","sense":"Debt — something owed; sin pictured as an unpaid debt to God.","anchor":"Matthew 6:12","en":"debts","text":"Forgive us our debts, as we also forgive our debtors."}]},{"id":"evil","name":"Evil & Malice","lang":"Greek","english":["evil","malice","wicked"],"intro":"English ‘evil’ hides two main Greek words. κακός describes what is bad in itself — worthless, harmful in nature. πονηρός describes evil that is active and aggressive, actively doing harm; it is used of ‘the evil one’. 1 Thessalonians 5 uses both: do not repay κακός for κακός (5:15), and abstain from every form of πονηρός (5:22).","members":[{"strongs":"G2556","sense":"Bad, evil in nature — worthless, harmful; what is wrong in itself.","anchor":"1 Thessalonians 5:15","en":"evil","text":"See that no one returns evil for evil to anyone, but always follow after that which is good, for one another, and for all."},{"strongs":"G4190","sense":"Evil in action — malicious, actively doing harm; ‘the evil one’.","anchor":"1 Thessalonians 5:22","en":"evil","text":"Abstain from every form of evil."},{"strongs":"G2549","sense":"Malice — badness of heart, ill will that wants harm for others.","anchor":"Colossians 3:8","en":"malice","text":"but now you also put them all away: anger, wrath, malice, slander, and shameful speaking out of your mouth."}]},{"id":"pray","name":"Prayer, Asking & Intercession","lang":"Greek","english":["pray","prayer","ask","petition","intercession"],"intro":"Several Greek words lie behind ‘pray’ and ‘ask’. In John 14:16 the WEB's ‘I will pray to the Father’ is ἐρωτάω — to ask, as one who speaks to the Father as an equal.","members":[{"strongs":"G4336","sense":"To pray to God — prayer as worship and communion, used only of prayer to God.","anchor":"Matthew 6:6","en":"pray","text":"But you, when you pray, enter into your inner room, and having shut your door, pray to your Father who is in secret, and your Father who sees in secret will reward you openly."},{"strongs":"G1162","sense":"Petition — a request rising out of a specific need.","anchor":"Philippians 4:6","en":"petition","text":"In nothing be anxious, but in everything, by prayer and petition with thanksgiving, let your requests be made known to God."},{"strongs":"G1189","sense":"To beg, to plead — the verb of δέησις: earnest, specific asking out of need.","anchor":"1 Thessalonians 3:10","en":"praying","text":"night and day praying exceedingly that we may see your face, and may perfect that which is lacking in your faith?"},{"strongs":"G154","sense":"To ask for something — a request from a lesser to a greater.","anchor":"Matthew 7:7","en":"Ask","text":"“Ask, and it will be given you. Seek, and you will find. Knock, and it will be opened for you."},{"strongs":"G2065","sense":"To ask, request — on equal footing; used of Jesus asking the Father.","anchor":"John 14:16","en":"pray","text":"I will pray to the Father, and he will give you another Counselor, that he may be with you forever,—"},{"strongs":"G1793","sense":"To intercede — to meet with someone on another's behalf.","anchor":"Hebrews 7:25","en":"intercession","text":"Therefore he is also able to save to the uttermost those who draw near to God through him, seeing that he lives forever to make intercession for them."}]},{"id":"good","name":"Good","lang":"Greek","english":["good"],"intro":"Greek distinguishes what is good in its effect from what is good and beautiful to look at.","members":[{"strongs":"G18","sense":"Good in nature and effect — beneficial, doing good.","anchor":"Romans 8:28","en":"good","text":"We know that all things work together for good for those who love God, to those who are called according to his purpose."},{"strongs":"G2570","sense":"Good and beautiful — noble, excellent, attractive; the Good Shepherd.","anchor":"John 10:11","en":"good","text":"I am the good shepherd. The good shepherd lays down his life for the sheep."}]},{"id":"see","name":"See, Look & Behold","lang":"Greek","english":["see","saw","look"],"intro":"John 20:5–8 uses three different verbs that the WEB translates ‘saw’: a glance, a careful gaze, and seeing that leads to understanding — ‘he saw and believed’.","members":[{"strongs":"G991","sense":"To look, to see with the eyes — the simple act of seeing.","anchor":"John 20:5","en":"saw","text":"Stooping and looking in, he saw the linen cloths lying, yet he didn’t enter in."},{"strongs":"G2334","sense":"To gaze, observe carefully — watching with attention (the root of ‘theatre’).","anchor":"John 20:6","en":"saw","text":"Then Simon Peter came, following him, and entered into the tomb. He saw the linen cloths lying,"},{"strongs":"G1492","sense":"To see and perceive — seeing that understands (Strong's files ‘saw’ and ‘know’ under one number).","anchor":"John 20:8","en":"saw","text":"So then the other disciple who came first to the tomb also entered in, and he saw and believed."},{"strongs":"G2300","sense":"To behold — looking intently and taking in what is seen.","anchor":"John 1:14","en":"saw","text":"The Word became flesh, and lived among us. We saw his glory, such glory as of the one and only Son of the Father, full of grace and truth."}]},{"id":"rise","name":"Rise, Raise & Resurrection","lang":"Greek","english":["raise","raised","rise","rose","resurrection"],"intro":"Two Greek verbs lie behind ‘raise’ and ‘rise’. ἐγείρω pictures waking someone up; ἀνίστημι pictures standing up again. 1 Thessalonians uses both: God ‘raised’ Jesus (1:10), Jesus ‘rose’ (4:14) and the dead in Christ will ‘rise’ (4:16). The noun ἀνάστασις, resurrection, comes from the second.","members":[{"strongs":"G1453","sense":"To wake, to rouse, to raise — often God raising Jesus, as one wakes a sleeper.","anchor":"1 Thessalonians 1:10","en":"raised","text":"and to wait for his Son from heaven, whom he raised from the dead—Jesus, who delivers us from the wrath to come."},{"strongs":"G450","sense":"To stand up, to rise again — the body standing up out of death.","anchor":"1 Thessalonians 4:14","en":"rose","text":"For if we believe that Jesus died and rose again, even so God will bring with him those who have fallen asleep in Jesus."},{"strongs":"G386","sense":"Resurrection — a standing up again from the dead.","anchor":"John 11:25","en":"resurrection","text":"Jesus said to her, “I am the resurrection and the life. He who believes in me will still live, even if he dies."}]},{"id":"sleep","name":"Sleep & Wakefulness","lang":"Greek","english":["sleep","asleep","sleeping","watch","wake"],"intro":"The New Testament uses two words for ‘sleep’. κοιμάω is the gentle word for believers who have died — they will wake. καθεύδω is ordinary sleep, and in 1 Thessalonians 5 the spiritual drowsiness of those who are not ready. Its opposite is γρηγορέω, to stay awake and watch. In 5:10 Paul uses ‘wake or sleep’ to mean living or having died.","members":[{"strongs":"G2837","sense":"To fall asleep — used of believers who have died, because death for them is temporary.","anchor":"John 11:11","en":"asleep","text":"He said these things, and after that, he said to them, “Our friend, Lazarus, has fallen asleep, but I am going so that I may awake him out of sleep.”"},{"strongs":"G2518","sense":"To sleep, lie down to rest — ordinary sleep; figuratively, spiritual drowsiness.","anchor":"Mark 5:39","en":"asleep","text":"When he had entered in, he said to them, “Why do you make an uproar and weep? The child is not dead, but is asleep.”"},{"strongs":"G1127","sense":"To stay awake, to watch — alert and ready; the opposite of spiritual sleep.","anchor":"Colossians 4:2","en":"watching","text":"Continue steadfastly in prayer, watching therein with thanksgiving;"}]},{"id":"god-names","name":"Names and Titles of God","lang":"Hebrew","english":["Yahweh","LORD","God","Lord","Armies","Almighty"],"intro":"The Old Testament uses several names and titles for God, and English Bibles often hide them behind ‘LORD’, ‘Lord’ and ‘God’. The WEB writes the personal name as ‘Yahweh’.","members":[{"strongs":"H3068","sense":"Yahweh — God's personal covenant name (written ‘LORD’ in most English Bibles).","anchor":"Malachi 3:6","en":"Yahweh","text":"“For I, Yahweh, don’t change; therefore you, sons of Jacob, are not consumed."},{"strongs":"H430","sense":"Elohim — God, the mighty Creator; plural in form, used with singular verbs for the one true God.","anchor":"Zephaniah 3:17","en":"God","text":"Yahweh, your God, is among you, a mighty one who will save. He will rejoice over you with joy. He will calm you in his love. He will rejoice over you with singing."},{"strongs":"H410","sense":"El — God, the Mighty One; often in compound titles (El Shaddai, El Elyon).","anchor":"Malachi 2:10","en":"God","text":"Don’t we all have one father? Hasn’t one God created us? Why do we deal treacherously every man against his brother, profaning the covenant of our fathers?"},{"strongs":"H136","sense":"Adonai — Lord, Master; God as sovereign owner.","anchor":"Zephaniah 1:7","en":"Lord","text":"Be silent at the presence of the Lord Yahweh, for the day of Yahweh is at hand. For Yahweh has prepared a sacrifice. He has consecrated his guests."},{"strongs":"H6635","sense":"Tsevaot — armies, hosts; ‘Yahweh of Armies’, commander of heaven's forces.","anchor":"Haggai 1:2","en":"Armies","text":"“This is what Yahweh of Armies says: These people say, ‘The time hasn’t yet come, the time for Yahweh’s house to be built.’”"},{"strongs":"H7706","sense":"Shaddai — the Almighty; God all-sufficient.","anchor":"Genesis 17:1","en":"Almighty","text":""}]},{"id":"sin-hebrew","name":"Sin, Iniquity & Transgression","lang":"Hebrew","english":["sin","iniquity","transgression","transgressions"],"intro":"Hebrew has three main words for wrongdoing, and Psalm 32:5 uses all three in one verse: sin, iniquity and transgressions.","members":[{"strongs":"H2403","sense":"Sin — missing the mark; also the sin offering that deals with it.","anchor":"Zechariah 13:1","en":"sin","text":"“In that day there will be a spring opened to David’s house and to the inhabitants of Jerusalem, for sin and for uncleanness."},{"strongs":"H5771","sense":"Iniquity — twistedness, perversity, and the guilt it carries.","anchor":"Zechariah 3:4","en":"iniquity","text":"He answered and spoke to those who stood before him, saying, “Take the filthy garments off him.” To him he said, “Behold, I have caused your iniquity to pass from you, and I will clothe you with rich clothing.”"},{"strongs":"H6588","sense":"Transgression — rebellion, deliberate revolt against God's authority.","anchor":"Psalm 32:5","en":"transgressions","text":""}]},{"id":"love-hebrew","name":"Love, Kindness & Compassion","lang":"Hebrew","english":["love","loved","kindness","compassion","grace"],"intro":"Hebrew describes God's love from several angles: choosing love, covenant loyalty, womb-deep compassion and undeserved favour. Zechariah 7:9 puts kindness and compassion side by side.","members":[{"strongs":"H157","sense":"To love — to choose and hold dear (God's love for Israel).","anchor":"Malachi 1:2","en":"loved","text":"“I have loved you,” says Yahweh. Yet you say, “How have you loved us?” “Wasn’t Esau Jacob’s brother?” says Yahweh, “Yet I loved Jacob;"},{"strongs":"H160","sense":"Love (noun) — affection, the love God quietly rests in over His people.","anchor":"Zephaniah 3:17","en":"love","text":"Yahweh, your God, is among you, a mighty one who will save. He will rejoice over you with joy. He will calm you in his love. He will rejoice over you with singing."},{"strongs":"H2617","sense":"Chesed — steadfast, loyal covenant love; kindness that keeps its promises.","anchor":"Zechariah 7:9","en":"kindness","text":"“Thus has Yahweh of Armies spoken, saying, ‘Execute true judgment, and show kindness and compassion every man to his brother."},{"strongs":"H7356","sense":"Compassion — tender mercy; related to the word for womb.","anchor":"Zechariah 7:9","en":"compassion","text":"“Thus has Yahweh of Armies spoken, saying, ‘Execute true judgment, and show kindness and compassion every man to his brother."},{"strongs":"H2580","sense":"Grace, favour — kindness shown to the undeserving.","anchor":"Zechariah 12:10","en":"grace","text":"I will pour on David’s house, and on the inhabitants of Jerusalem, the spirit of grace and of supplication; and they will look to me whom they have pierced; and they shall mourn for him, as one mourns for his only son, and will grieve bitterly for him, as one grieves for his firstborn."}]},{"id":"power-hebrew","name":"Strength & Might","lang":"Hebrew","english":["might","power","mighty","strong","strength"],"intro":"Zechariah 4:6 sets two Hebrew strength-words against the Spirit: ‘Not by might, nor by power’.","members":[{"strongs":"H2428","sense":"Might — force, army, wealth; the strength of resources and numbers.","anchor":"Zechariah 4:6","en":"might","text":"Then he answered and spoke to me, saying, “This is Yahweh’s word to Zerubbabel, saying, ‘Not by might, nor by power, but by my Spirit,’ says Yahweh of Armies."},{"strongs":"H3581","sense":"Power — personal strength, the ability to do.","anchor":"Zechariah 4:6","en":"power","text":"Then he answered and spoke to me, saying, “This is Yahweh’s word to Zerubbabel, saying, ‘Not by might, nor by power, but by my Spirit,’ says Yahweh of Armies."},{"strongs":"H1368","sense":"Mighty one — a warrior, a hero; God as champion.","anchor":"Zephaniah 3:17","en":"mighty","text":"Yahweh, your God, is among you, a mighty one who will save. He will rejoice over you with joy. He will calm you in his love. He will rejoice over you with singing."},{"strongs":"H2388","sense":"To be strong — to take hold, be firm, be courageous.","anchor":"Haggai 2:4","en":"strong","text":"Yet now be strong, Zerubbabel,’ says Yahweh. ‘Be strong, Joshua, son of Jehozadak, the high priest. Be strong, all you people of the land,’ says Yahweh, ‘and work, for I am with you,’ says Yahweh of Armies."},{"strongs":"H5797","sense":"Strength — might, security, stronghold.","anchor":"Psalm 46:1","en":"strength","text":""}]},{"id":"time-hebrew","name":"Time, Day & Forever","lang":"Hebrew","english":["time","day","feasts","forever"],"intro":"Hebrew distinguishes the season for something, the day, the appointed time and the long age.","members":[{"strongs":"H6256","sense":"Time, season — the right time for something.","anchor":"Haggai 1:2","en":"time","text":"“This is what Yahweh of Armies says: These people say, ‘The time hasn’t yet come, the time for Yahweh’s house to be built.’”"},{"strongs":"H3117","sense":"Day — a literal day, and ‘the day of Yahweh’.","anchor":"Zephaniah 1:14","en":"day","text":"The great day of Yahweh is near. It is near, and hurries greatly, the voice of the day of Yahweh. The mighty man cries there bitterly."},{"strongs":"H4150","sense":"Appointed time — a fixed meeting or feast.","anchor":"Zechariah 8:19","en":"feasts","text":"Yahweh of Armies says: “The fasts of the fourth, fifth, seventh, and tenth months shall be for the house of Judah joy and gladness, and cheerful feasts. Therefore love truth and peace.”"},{"strongs":"H5769","sense":"Olam — age, long duration, forever.","anchor":"Malachi 1:4","en":"forever","text":"Whereas Edom says, “We are beaten down, but we will return and build the waste places”; Yahweh of Armies says, “They shall build, but I will throw down; and men will call them ‘The Wicked Land,’ even the people against whom Yahweh shows wrath forever.”"}]}];
